From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: the user's UserChoice decides a file type's or protocol's program

Windows opens a file with the program the user chose -- the ProgId in
HKCU\...\Explorer\FileExts\.ext\UserChoice -- before the class the
extension names, and a URL with the one in the Shell Associations'
UrlAssociations\<protocol>\UserChoice. Wine read neither for files and only
QueryCurrentDefault read the protocol's. SHELL_GetUserChoice (only a
registered ProgId counts; Windows' hash of the choice is not checked) is
now consulted by IQueryAssociations::Init (AssocQueryString and every
IQueryAssociations user), its command lookup (which took the extension's
own class even when another was chosen), ShellExecute and FindExecutable
for files and URLs, the context menu's class and QueryCurrentDefault.

Gate: test/hkcr-gate.sh.
